{
  "extends": "@vue/tsconfig/tsconfig.dom.json",
  "compilerOptions": {
    "tsBuildInfoFile": "./node_modules/.tmp/tsconfig.app.tsbuildinfo",
    "types": ["vite/client"],

    // DELTA from create-vite-extra@5.0.2 template-ssr-vue-ts/tsconfig.app.json,
    // and the only compiler option this demo changes. `@vue/tsconfig` sets
    // neither, so the scaffold default is `allowJs: false`.
    //
    // THE PREMISE THIS BLOCK CARRIED WAS FALSE, AND IT WAS LOAD-BEARING. It said
    // "the three components in src/emitted" carry NO `lang="ts"`, so vue-tsc saw
    // them as JS modules and `allowJs` was what let it read them at all. There
    // are EIGHT emitted components, and ALL of them have carried `lang="ts"`
    // since the extension/lang migration. vue-tsc therefore READS AND CHECKS
    // them as TypeScript, which is the opposite of what this comment claimed and
    // is why `allowJs` is no longer the thing keeping them visible.
    //
    // `allowJs` STAYS anyway: the scaffold default is `allowJs: false`, and
    // nothing here has re-measured whether the rest of the demo tolerates
    // flipping it. Removing it is a separate change with its own evidence, not a
    // tidy-up ridden along with this one.
    //
    // `checkJs` stays off, and unlike demos/svelte-official's identical pair this
    // was MEASURED at both settings rather than inherited. Turning it ON buys
    // exactly ZERO additional coverage and costs exactly the noise class
    // packages/frameworks/solid/test/emitted-typecheck.test.ts predicts in its
    // own header — six errors on src/emitted/EventForm.vue alone, all of the form
    // "'event.target' is possibly 'null'" and "Property 'dataset' does not exist
    // on type 'EventTarget'", which are properties of type-checking untyped JS
    // and not emitter defects. Emitted output IS checked, by its own package's
    // lane: packages/frameworks/vue/test/compile-emitted.test.ts runs
    // @vue/compiler-sfc parse + compileScript + compileTemplate and requires
    // errors AND tips to be an exact empty set across ssr x dev/prod.
    //
    // WHAT vue-tsc ACTUALLY COVERS HERE. RE-RUN rather than edited, at BOTH
    // checkJs settings, with identical results at each:
    //
    //   unknown prop on an emitted component      MISSED  (unchanged)
    //   wrong-typed prop on an emitted component  CAUGHT  <- THIS ROW FLIPPED
    //   undefined identifier in App.vue           CAUGHT  (unchanged)
    //   wrong-typed use of a typed local          CAUGHT  (unchanged)
    //
    // EACH ROW IS A DELTA AGAINST THE BASELINE, NOT AN EXIT CODE, because the
    // baseline is ALREADY RED — see below. Reading exit codes here would report
    // all four rows RED and measure nothing.
    //
    // ROW 2 IS THE ONE THAT MOVED, and it is the prop hole closing. It was GREEN
    // because `defineProps(['label', …])` types every prop `any`. The emitted
    // RenderOnce.vue now declares its props at RUNTIME —
    // `{ label: { type: String, required: true }, … }` — built from IR-8's
    // authored type AND its authored requiredness, so a wrong-typed binding in
    // App.vue is now `TS2322: Type 'number' is not assignable to type 'string'`.
    // `required` is what makes this reachable: with bare constructors every prop
    // is optional and the emitted component's OWN script fails strict TS.
    //
    // ROW 1 IS STILL MISSED, and no amount of prop typing will close it: Vue
    // lets an undeclared prop fall through to attrs rather than erroring. That
    // is a framework rule, not a gap in this config or in IR-8.
    //
    // ONLY RenderOnce IS COVERED. It is the corpus's ONLY annotated module, so
    // it is the only emitted component whose props carry types at all; the other
    // seven still emit the array form and still type every prop `any`.
    //
    // THE BASELINE IS RED AND WAS RED BEFORE ANY OF THIS. `vue-tsc -b` reports
    // 40 diagnostics over the SEVEN unannotated emitted components — TS7006
    // implicit-any parameters, TS18047 possibly-null event targets, TS2339 on
    // EventTarget — byte-for-byte the same list before and after the runtime
    // declaration landed, and NONE of them in RenderOnce.vue. They are the noise
    // class packages/frameworks/solid/test/emitted-typecheck.test.ts predicts,
    // and they appeared when the emitted SFCs gained `lang="ts"`.
    //
    // AND `pnpm e2e` DOES NOT SEE ANY OF IT. e2e runs this demo's `copy-emitted`
    // script and then the witness against the dev server; it never runs `build`,
    // so `vue-tsc -b` is never invoked on this lane. A green e2e is therefore
    // NOT evidence that this project type-checks — recorded because treating it
    // as such is exactly this board's recurring proxy-for-measurement fault.
    "allowJs": true,
    "checkJs": false,

    /* Linting */
    "noUnusedLocals": true,
    "noUnusedParameters": true,
    "erasableSyntaxOnly": true,
    "noFallthroughCasesInSwitch": true
  },
  "include": ["src/**/*.ts", "src/**/*.tsx", "src/**/*.vue"]
}
